      "id": 1,
      "text": "Breesport, New York, experienced rapid growth in the late nineteenth century, largely due to the contributions of the Rodbourn family.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breesport%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first steam-powered mill in Breesport was built in 1857 by Joseph Rodbourn, producing three million feet of lumber yearly.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breesport%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1830, the Heller family established the first sawmill in Breesport, just two years after settling in the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breesport%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Breesport's first store was created in 1855 by Ulysses and William R. Breese, brothers of the town's namesake, Azariah Breese.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breesport%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Adam Kinley, a notable economic leader in Breesport, developed several brickyards along Newton Creek during the late nineteenth century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
